A few things to know about TransAmiga:

TransAmiga has a few features you may wish to know about.  You can
retrieve lines that you have previously entered into the BBS by pressing
CTRL-K, TransAmiga keeps track of the last 20 commands you entered.  You
can also erase the current line completely by pressing CTRL-X.  If your
terminal has ANSI graphic capabilities, it is recommended you turn ANSI
on, then you can also use the cursor keys, the backspace key and the
delete key to edit the current line.  ANSI users can also use the
full-screen editor for writing messages.

When you enter commands in TransAmiga, you must press RETURN at the end of
a line.  However, you can "stack" several commands on one line, and
TransAmiga will process the entire batch at once.  If you prefer, however,
you may switch to hotkeys, where commands are processed immediately
without pressing RETURN.

At just about any menu, you can press "H" to get explanations about
available commands.

